# Accessibility

Follow `.cursor/skills/accessibility/SKILL.md` on every UI, form, or route change.

- Semantic HTML; no clickable `div` stand-ins for buttons or links
- A real label on every form input (write desk is used by a non-technical person)
- Alt text for recipe photos; empty alt only for decorative art
- WCAG 2.1 AA contrast; visible `:focus-visible`; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Primary controls ≥ 44×44px on mobile; nothing hidden behind the bottom dock
- Verify desktop 1280×800 and mobile 390×844
- Add or update an a11y test (`tests/a11y.spec.ts`) for new pages or interactive components
- Fail on serious/critical axe violations; do not disable rules or skip tests
- If a surface cannot be reached without a live Convex backend, say so in the PR
- Prove it works on the real page (axe + keyboard + tap targets), not “it compiles”
- Never include any person's name in site content
